# Round 19 (GD-2 beside it): L §4.2 schedule(p, e, roll, cal) "the day of period p given by e (an int day of the
# month, p a month; a day in every year is `schedule(month_of(start_of(y)) + (pay_month - 1), pay_dom, roll, cal)`)":
# p is a month. snap14 still took schedule(y, md) of a year with a month-day literal (A-49 had removed it); a year is
# a value of the wrong type (LOAD-UNIT).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2026..2027
input file_by: monthday
input other: monthday
input pd: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  file_by = 04-30
  other = 04-30
  pd = 5
ask q: schedule(2026, pd, following, calendar(weekends [sat, sun]))
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT schedule takes a month, not year (m.tally:21)
